    "description": "Lionel Postwar O Gauge Flatcar Lot - 2 Pieces With Original Boxes\nNo. 6801 Flatcar with Boat & No. 6477 Bulkhead Flatcar with Pipe Load\nPostwar Era, Made in USA\nThis vintage lot features two classic Postwar Lionel O gauge freight cars accompanied by their original boxes. Included are the No. 6801 flatcar equipped with its white cradle and blue-and-white plastic cabin cruiser boat, along with the No. 6477 bulkhead flatcar carrying a structural pipe load secured between side stakes. Produced during the late 1950s, these workhorse freight cars showcase the ingenuity and charm of Lionel's golden era of model railroading.\nLionel No. 6801 red flatcar with white cradle and blue/white runabout boat marked 6801-50\nLionel No. 6477 red bulkhead flatcar with black end racks, vertical side stakes, and pipe load\nBoth cars feature operational knuckle couplers and die-cast metal trucks\nIncludes two original Lionel Corporation classic orange-and-blue illustrated boxes\nCondition:\nFlatcars display light play wear consistent with age, including faint surface scuffs and light oxidation on metal axles and couplers. The boat shows mild dust accumulation and age-related toning to the cream plastic deck. Pipe load exhibits minor surface marks. Both boxes have shelf wear, edge creasing, and flap wear, with one box missing end flaps. Complete as pictured.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
